{
  "$schema": "./SCHEMA.md#recovery-approval",
  "description": "A guardian's approval of a recovery (avalon_protocol::identity_id::recovery_approval_signing_bytes): tag avalon.recovery.approval, layout version 1, fields network_id (str), the recovering identity_id (32 raw bytes), request_id (uuid, also the id of the new signing key), the guardian's identity id (32 raw bytes), the guardian's signing_key_id (uuid), the new public key (algorithm byte + 32 raw bytes), the 32-byte ledger entry hash of the identity.recovery_requested marker, the 32-byte chain hash of the identity.recovery_configured event relied on, and the guardian's chain position (seq u64, hash algorithm byte, prev_hash flag byte then 32 bytes when present). The position is the seq the guardian's next chained event would take; the guardian's key is judged at it from the guardian's own accepted chain. The guardian signs with their own key and approves nothing but this recovery to this key. identity.recovered embeds at least the threshold of these approvals. Here identityId is the recovering identity and the signer is the guardian (signingKeySeedHex stands in for the guardian key). The layout is the structured signing-bytes encoding (avalon_protocol::signing_bytes): the ASCII domain tag with no length, a u16 big-endian layout version (1) and a u32 big-endian rules version (1), then the fields in the order listed, then the extensions region (count u16 = 0: 00 00). str is a u32 big-endian byte length and the UTF-8 bytes; uuid is its 16 raw bytes; identity ids are 32 raw bytes; a public key is the algorithm byte 01 (Ed25519) then its 32 raw bytes; seq is a u64 big-endian, followed by the hash algorithm byte 01 (SHA-256) and prev_hash, one byte (0 = no previous event, 1 = a 32-byte event hash follows). The signature is Ed25519 by the signer key over the bytes, verified strictly. replayVectors offer a signature made for one input with another input's bytes; it must not verify. There is no legacy layout.",
  "generation": "Generated by scripts/gen-identity-key-event-vectors.py, an encoder that shares no code with the Rust one (cryptography Ed25519, hashlib). signingKeySeedHex is the Ed25519 seed of the signer; Ed25519 signatures are deterministic.",
